# ArchLex Dynamic CDN Icon Loading Configuration
# See docs/guides/dynamic-cdn-icons.md for detailed documentation

# Icon Cache Configuration
# -------------------------

# Directory where icons are cached persistently (default: ~/.cache/archlex/icons)
# ARCHLEX_ICON_CACHE_DIR=/custom/cache/path

# Time-to-live for cached icons in days (default: 7)
# ARCHLEX_ICON_CACHE_TTL=30

# Disable CDN icon loading completely (default: false)
# When enabled, only bundled icons will be used
# ARCHLEX_DISABLE_CDN_ICONS=true

# Debug Configuration
# --------------------

# Enable debug logging for icon loading (set to "icons" to enable)
# ARCHLEX_DEBUG=icons

# Custom CDN URLs (Optional)
# ---------------------------

# Override AWS icon CDN base URL
# ARCHLEX_AWS_ICON_CDN_URL=https://custom-aws-cdn.com/icons

# Override GCP icon CDN base URL
# ARCHLEX_GCP_ICON_CDN_URL=https://custom-gcp-cdn.com/svg

# Notes:
# ------
# - Default cache directory: ~/.cache/archlex/icons
# - Default TTL: 7 days
# - Icons are fetched from CDN only in Node.js environments
# - Browser environments (playground) use bundled icons only
# - Cache uses atomic file operations for data integrity
# - Security-hardened SVG sanitization prevents XSS/XXE attacks
